WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.250
Each output supports a specific control
from the guide's requirements table.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.501
Each policy's mode, body inspection,

3
00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:11.858
rule sets and rate limit support NIST's
information input validation and boundary

4
00:00:11.858 --> 00:00:17.137
protection controls, aligned to a FedRAMP
indicator that cites input validation.

5
00:00:17.137 --> 00:00:22.004
Every internet-facing endpoint behind
a WAF in prevention, the plan reviewed

6
00:00:22.004 --> 00:00:27.100
before it runs, and the logs from every
endpoint all support boundary protection.

7
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.200
The kit's output supports these
controls; the assessor decides.
